# Copy to .env in the directory you start the server from. The server reads it
# (and a .env in up to four parent folders) at startup, when it picks a model.
# A real environment variable always wins. Write plain KEY=VALUE lines, with no
# comment after the value.

# --- Chat model ---
# The first key that is set wins, in this order: Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini.
# With no key the server uses a local Ollama model (llama3.1:8b).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OpenAI and Gemini also need their extra: pip install "aigenos-flow[openai]"
# or "aigenos-flow[gemini]". OPENAI_BASE_URL points OpenAI at a compatible
# endpoint. FG_MODEL overrides the model name; for Ollama it must be a tag
# with a colon.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# FG_MODEL=

# --- Widget generator (the Studio's widget designer) ---
# Uses Anthropic when ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set, otherwise Ollama if it answers
# at OLLAMA_HOST. FLOW_AI_PROVIDER forces one: anthropic or ollama.
# FLOW_AI_PROVIDER=
# FLOW_ANTHROPIC_MODEL=
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=

# --- Read before this file is loaded: set these in your shell instead ---
# FG_PORT           port for `python -m aigenos_flow.main` (default 8000).
#                   With uvicorn, pass --port.
# FG_SKILLS_DIR     the skills folder /flow serves. Default in a clone:
#                   examples/studio_agent/skills.
# FG_MODE           interpreter mode: flex (default) or strict.
# FG_CORS_ORIGINS   comma-separated browser origins. Default: localhost and
#                   127.0.0.1 on ports 5173 and 3000.
# FG_DATA_DIR       widgets, workflows and the workspace database. Defaults to
#                   a folder inside the installed package, which may be
#                   read-only, so point it at a writable path.
